\section{Architecture and prior-art boundary}
Fusion v2 is a persistence-anchored, horizon-conditioned custom adaptation:
separate short, medium, and slow \cn{} streams; weather conditioning inside
the temporal representation; derived stability/refractivity tokens; a
four-expert diagnostic router; quantiles and a heavy-tailed Student-\(t\)
head; and masked-weather/future-weather/cadence-aware pretraining. Temporal
Fusion Transformers motivate interpretable temporal selection
\cite{lim2020tft}; PatchTST motivates patchwise multivariate representation
\cite{nie2023patchtst}; TimeXer is close prior art for endogenous/exogenous
interaction \cite{wang2024timexer}; OTBench supplies the public benchmark
context \cite{otbench}. This exact implementation is described as a
custom adaptation, not a universal novelty claim.

